    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Enslaved as a teenager in the Islamic world and Embraced circa 750 CE by Abd ar-Rahman, Jacob is a fifth-generation @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.ZJx9H3XnU8yQGy9s]{Malkavian} elder secretly living in Milwaukee under two identities. As Jacob, he keeps a mansion on the fringe of Kindred territory in Greendale; as Esau, a split personality he created upon his Embrace, he keeps a condo north of downtown. The two personalities wage a private, decades-long war against one another using unwitting Kindred pawns (notably Turk of the Union, whom Esau has secretly Dominated). Jacob claims the Jyhad is a fiction and that all Kindred conflict is mundane rivalry; whichever mask he is wearing, his true goal is always the destruction of the other. Most Kindred who become entangled in the Jacob/Esau war die quickly, as each side always seems to know the other's plans.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Charming, paternal, and utterly insane beneath a distinguished veneer. Try to recruit anyone you meet into your side of the war against \"my brother.\" Flatter, coax, and threaten as needed, but let your conversation grow subtly disjointed the longer it continues.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Abd ar-Rahman. Havens: a mansion in Greendale (as Jacob) and a condo north of downtown (as Esau). Disciplines as printed: Auspex 6, Dominate 5, Obfuscate 5, Presence 6 (capped above to this system's 1-5 scale). Signature powers: Insight of the Mad (Auspex) and Coax (Presence), used together to compel others toward his hidden agenda.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
